  "after": "## What to take from it\n- **Deny is checked first, everywhere.** A narrow allow cannot open a hole in a broad deny.\n- **An allow must cover every part** of a compound command; a deny or ask needs only one part.\n- **Rules match text, not programs.** `git -C . push` slips past `Bash(git push *)`: treat deny rules as guard rails, and use the sandbox or a hook where a hard boundary matters.\n- **The mode is the fallback.** The same unmatched command asks in Manual, goes to the classifier in auto, and is refused in don't ask.\n\nThe [[tool:permissions|permissions tool]] runs the same check against your own rules."
