  "after": "## What to take from it\n- **Adding is safe provider-first.** A new optional field or endpoint breaks nobody until a consumer needs it, so ship the provider, then the consumers.\n- **Renaming breaks in both simple orders.** Provider first strands the old consumer; consumer first asks for a field that is not there yet. Expand, migrate, contract never breaks.\n- **Removing is safe consumer-first.** Stop using it everywhere, prove nothing reads it, then delete it.\n- **Making something required** is a rename in disguise: accept it as optional first, have every consumer send it, then require it.\n- **Merged is not deployed.** Each step waits for the previous deploy, not the previous merge."
